hi I'm Evan Carmichael welcome to  another edition of ask Evan now last  month I put out a call on YouTube asking  for questions from readers that we're  gonna answer on this channel for our  video here in December and we got so  many questions I'm gonna pick the top  three that I really liked and we're  gonna answer them now here today and  then I'm gonna be answering more as part  of our challenge Series in 2013 so three  of the questions that I got asked I'm  gonna pull them up here and got my  Samsung Galaxy Note 2 that I've got some  questions on so the first one is from  one of our YouTube viewers when were you  the happiest thanks for you inspirations  don't stop making videos I'll keep  making these videos as long as you guys  keep watching the videos in terms of  what makes me happiest I'm happiest when  I'm helping entrepreneurs and that may  sound really cheesy or corny but that  that's what that's what drives me I love  helping entrepreneurs and I think a big  problem is a lot of entrepreneurs don't  start asking for help until it's almost  too late  you know they've tried everything on  their own they're at their wit's end  they're frustrated exasperated out of  money and don't know what to do next you  know thinking about quitting giving up  and they come to me and they ask you  their questions as kind of a last resort  and I'm able to help them and seeing  their eyes light up that a you know  somebody believes in you and thinks you  can accomplish it and also has given you  some practical suggestions and advice to  help you grow your business that's  awesome  like seeing somebody light up like that  makes my day I wish I could do it all  day long I try to do it as much as I can  as part of my business and so whether  it's you know face to face or trying to  make videos like this for you guys or  over the phone or at a conference or  speaking event I love helping  entrepreneurs and try to incorporate  that as much as I can again into my day  to day life so we you know whatever it  is for you you want to find that passion  unfortunately I found that relatively  early on and I can try to live that and  do that everyday and hopefully some of  the excitement and passions coming  through in this videos I'm talking to  you but that's what really drives me and  that's that's when I'm happiest so  hopefully you find that happening  for your business as well so thanks for  that question flushing number one okay  so we're gonna turn the question number  two now comes from one of our readers  skip  so skip wrote in say my main question is  getting seed or startup cash whether I  sell shares of my company to people I  know or go to a VC who might be able to  help my business along because of their  expertise connections etc thanks for the  question skip very common question for  entrepreneurs who are starting up trying  to get the money to grow their company  the first thing I would think about is  do you really really really absolutely  need the money to start this business  the couple reasons why I ask that the  first is raising capital almost becomes  a full-time job for your company so what  it does is take away your time to focus  on actually building up your company so  if you're out spending all this time  meeting VCS and meeting you know  individual investors friends family  angels whatever it is that's time that  you're not being you know I'm not  putting into actually growing your  business so do you absolutely need that  money to get going or is there a way  that you can bootstrap it up at least  get their certain point and then look at  raising capital should be easier the  second component to that is it's you're  gonna get killed in your valuation the  valuation on the startup is way way way  worse than if you have even one customer  a little bit of money coming into your  company when I was in the VC business we  got tons and tons and tons of proposals  and most of them were just an idea and  it's really hard for you to stand out  against everybody else that the fear is  that you're not gonna be able to make it  anybody can spend money right if I gave  you I don't know what you're looking for  or five hundred thousand dollars a  million dollars if I gave that to you  you could spend it right anybody can  spend it it's hard to make the money and  it's hard for you to stand out from  everybody else who's promising the same  thing as you are so if you're able to  build up your business at least a  certain point I'm not gonna expect you  to build a gigantic business all on your  own bootstrapping it up but if you can  get some customers and find ways to save  cost and grow a little bit of a business  and get some momentum going behind you  then when you go to investors where  those VCS or friends and family or  angels  it'll a be much easier to get them to  say yes because the easiest money to  raises expansion capital instead of  startup capital but also you get a much  better valuation so you're not giving up  as much of the business  you would if you need that money all  upfront so something to think about if  you really really need that money or not  I'd really encourage you to try to  bootstrap it up as much as you can  before going for investment if you have  to go for investment the next thing  guard look at if you're comparing  friends and family and angels to VCS the  first is how much of an active role do  you want somebody to play in your  business so obviously if you're going  with a VC partner you want somebody who  can bring connections and you know  contacts and partnerships and media and  customers to your business it's ideally  much better than somebody who's just  giving you money the the range will  depend on how much money you need to  grow your business right if you need  $100,000 for your company you're not  really going to be able to attract a  venture capital investor to come on for  that it's not it's too low you're  looking at a friends and family or  angels so I don't know how much you need  and if you're looking for half a million  or a million dollars then you're playing  in BC territory and you know unless you  have really really wealthy friends they  probably won't be able to afford a half  a million or a million dollar price tag  so right away depending on how much  money you need that's gonna depend on  you know who you end up going after then  you want to think about how much you get  involvement you want them to have in  your business so if you're going for  friends and family you know it's all  great when the business is going well  but business doesn't always go super  well right so if you have Uncle Joe  putting money into your company and it's  not going well for him then it's not  gonna make Thanksgiving dinner really  uncomfortable because Uncle Joe you know  was losing money on your business or  maybe he wants to really be involved in  your company but doesn't have any skill  sets that could you know you could  really use so you know do you want to  have him as part of your management team  or not some questions that you want to  ask yourself but definitely you want  ideally if you are going for an investor  somebody who can bring on more than just  money and can bring on connections and  experience and can complement some of  the weaknesses that you might have as an  entrepreneur one last tip about raising  capital if you know you need a certain  amount to say you need half a million  dollars your company I try to phase it  out so instead of saying half a million  dollars right now I try to phase it out  with milestones so say you need a  hundred thousand dollars now and then in  three months another two  and three months for the 200,000 you can  go to an investor and say this is how  much I need and this is what I'm gonna  need it phase out over a period of time  and if we hit certain milestones it  could be revenue targets a number of  customers or whatever it is that makes  sense for the business then you can ask  for better valuation so instead of  giving up a big chunkier company for  that half a million dollars now you can  give up you know only a little bit at  that hundred thousand dollars startup  and then in three months you've hit your  milestones you get another 200k at a  better evaluation and another few months  you get the final 200k and an even  better valuation because you've hit your  milestones and have shown your investor  that you're not just gonna be every  other startup that fizzles out so you're  reducing the risk for the investor and  you're also giving yourself a better  valuation and you're betting on yourself  you're saying yeah I'm gonna be able to  hit these targets and so by doing that  you're gonna get a much better price for  your company so a couple things to keep  in mind skip good luck with the business  and if you have other questions let me  know on to question number three  all right so question number three comes  from another one of our readers neo  cobby so he wrote in I have a question  I'm working for two companies I'm doing  a beauty salon and part-time marketing  at an events company in both companies I  am responsible for attracting new  clients to the business what is the best  and most efficient way to do this and  make it cost-effective so thank you for  the question another great question you  know as entrepreneurs we don't have a  lot of money to invest into our our  efforts so we want to make sure that the  money we're putting in is being spent as  wisely as possible and I hate spending  money until I'm making money and if  there was a rule for entrepreneurship  that would be one of them is don't spend  until you earn so I try to bootstrap it  I put them in your time but not start  spending a lot of money until you find a  way to make money and if you can do that  on a small scale then you invest your  money into making it more successful for  attracting new clients my favorite way  to do it is through partnerships so  going out and cold calling and doing  advertising and  you know calling on people going to  events can be a very time-consuming  process very expensive very slow and you  have to go through the process of  educating customers on why they should  come to you where if you're going  through a partner it's super fast and  can be very cost effective because  you're basically finding people who are  already selling to your target market  so you find somebody who's selling to  your ideal client and you strike up a  partnership or in agreement with them so  that can range from giving them a cut of  the sales or just you know something as  goodwill giving them an option for their  clients or you're gonna be referring  business back to them as well you  basically I look at who are people who  are also selling to your target market  and ideally what you look at is not  direct competitors because why would  they refer customers to you but you're  looking at people who where are they  buying before they buy from you  so this events management company who  are they buying from before they come to  you  maybe it's an event planner so then you  want to partner up with event planners  alright so think through that buying  process where are they buying from  before they end up coming to you and  start talking to those people and check  up partnership agreements with them so  they already have your target market  they're there selling to them they have  a relationship with them and so when  they say you got to work with this  company there's an incentive to want to  do it because they've been referred in  and referred clients ask us questions  I'm more qualified buy more are more  loyal stay with you longer spend more  money it's the best have a client to get  so you want to start making those  partnerships with similar companies who  can you know be very synergistic with  the same types of clients that you have  so that would be my number one tip on  the marketing side in terms of being  something cost-effective and also being  fast to get the market hopefully that  helps thank you guys for joining us for  another video we're gonna have a lot  more coming in 2013 if you like the  video please give it a thumbs up below I  love seeing those come out and if you  have a comment or question feel free to  leave it below in the comment section I  always read those I love seeing them and  I always apply as  fast as I can not always immediate but  as fast as I can so thank you have a  great end to the year and we'll see you  in 2013  you
 

